  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-107299",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the volume of one tank:  \n\n$$\n\\frac{375\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}}{3}=125\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of a single tank.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{125}=5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $5\\,\\text{m}.$",
